# Coding style guides

- Adhere to standard PHP coding styles enforced by PHP CodeSniffer (PSR2 and PHPDoc rules)
- Adhere to Yii’s MVC architecture. Controllers, models, and views should be organized and follow the repository pattern
- Separation of Concerns: Maintain clear boundaries between different parts of the application
- Use Docker and environment variables to manage deployment-specific configurations
- Adhere to WCAG 2.2 standards for the user interface
- Avoid making files longer than 300 lines
- Avoid creating functions longer than 30 lines